.. than</span> to express a comparison between two things.</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">She'd rather eat her own food than someone else's.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "She would prefer to eat food she likes and prepares herself. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "She would rather keep busy. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "She'd choose a book over TV any day.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "lifetime", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the length of time that we live ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: To the young, 83 seems like a lifetime away. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le11ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about the elderly.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "advanced", "type": "name"}, {"content": "high in number ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Do people at such advanced ages still have meaningful lives?  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le11ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "meaningful ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "important or valuable  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She led a highly productive, meaningful life. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le11ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to prepare", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make; get something ready ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He eats food he prepares himself. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le11ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "sparingly"